Narrative Version
Conversational AI in contact centers has crossed from experimentation to broad deployment, but not to consistent enterprise value. The market is big because labor is big, and software now has a credible path to absorb work previously done by agents. In healthcare, the timing is especially strong because interoperability and transparency requirements are making legacy manual processes less defensible.
The winning pattern is not “replace agents.” It is “automate routine, augment complex, and escalate seamlessly.” End users are clearly asking for faster and more fluid service across voice, chat, and media-rich interactions, but they still want control and access to a human when stakes are high.
For entry, a healthcare-first wedge with hard KPI economics is the least risky path: prior auth and member/patient service. Do this with strict governance and explicit transparency, and you can expand from one workflow into a broader cross-industry CX automation platform.
